---
/**
 * About / Our Story — copy from pages-content/_ about - Our Story.docx.
 * Poster layout. Photos come from the Sanity "About" singleton (`aboutContent`);
 * a missing photo renders the grey photo frame.
 */
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import PosterButton from '~/components/home/PosterButton.astro';
import HomePhoto from '~/components/home/HomePhoto.astro';
import Lanterns from '~/components/home/Lanterns.astro';
import ArtFlourish from '~/assets/images/v3/art-flourish.svg';
import ArtCactus from '~/assets/images/v3/art-cactus.svg';
import ArtAgave from '~/assets/images/v3/art-agave.svg';
import Blossom from '~/components/home/Blossom.astro';
import { getAboutImages } from '~/lib/content';

const images = await getAboutImages();

const metadata = {
  title: 'Our Story | Taqueria El Ranchero in Oʻahu',
  description:
    'Learn about Taqueria El Ranchero’s Northern California taqueria influence, ranchero-style dishes, daily preparation, and two Oʻahu locations.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
---

<PageLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <div class="v3-interior">
    <section class="v3-menu-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <Lanterns class="v3-menu-lanterns" />
      <div class="v3-wrap v3-menu-hero-frame">
        <div class="v3-menu-hero-copy">
          <h1 id="about-title" class="v3-display">
            About Taqueria<br />
            El Ranchero
          </h1>
          <div class="v3-menu-copy flex flex-col gap-4">
            <p>
              At Taqueria El Ranchero, we bring Northern California-inspired Mexican taqueria cooking to Oʻahu. Our
              approach centers on ranchero-style food, fresh daily preparation and meals made for everyday dining.
            </p>
            <p>
              From our original restaurant in Wahiawa to our newer location in Kapolei, we focus on the straightforward
              cooking that defines our taqueria style.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="v3-menu-hero-media">
          <HomePhoto
            image={images.hero}
            class="v3-menu-hero-photo"
            sizes="(min-width: 768px) 48vw, 100vw"
            loading="eager"
            fetchpriority="high"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="our-story" class="v3-section v3-paper v3-center" aria-labelledby="our-story-title">
      <Blossom class="v3-art v3-art-bloom-explore" fill="var(--v3-red)" center="var(--v3-red)" />
      <ArtAgave class="v3-art v3-art-agave" aria-hidden="true" />
      <div class="v3-wrap">
        <div class="v3-ihead">
          <h2 id="our-story-title" class="v3-display">Our Story</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="v3-prose">
          <p>
            Taqueria El Ranchero takes its inspiration from the Mexican taquerias of Northern California, where familiar
            dishes and simple preparation are central to the experience.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our first restaurant opened in Wahiawa, serving the surrounding neighborhood and people traveling through
            Central Oʻahu. We later expanded to Kapolei at Ka Makana Aliʻi, bringing the same menu to a full-service
            dining setting.
          </p>
          <p>
            Today, both restaurants share the same approach to food. Whether you’re visiting our <a
              href="/locations/wahiawa">Wahiawa location</a
            > or dining with us in <a href="/locations/kapolei">Kapolei</a>, you’ll find the tacos, burritos and
            ranchero-style dishes that define El Ranchero.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="ranchero-style" class="v3-section v3-red-band v3-center" aria-labelledby="ranchero-style-title">
      <div class="v3-wrap">
        <div class="v3-ihead">
          <h2 id="ranchero-style-title" class="v3-display">Ranchero Style</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="v3-prose">
          <p>
            The word ranchero refers to ranch-style cooking. For us, that means straightforward meals built around
            familiar ingredients such as chicken, beef, pork, rice and beans.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our food follows a Northern California taqueria approach rather than Tex-Mex or fusion cooking. We focus on
            recognizable dishes prepared with traditional combinations of meats, vegetables, tortillas and salsa.
          </p>
          <p>
            That approach runs throughout our menu, from everyday tacos and burritos to our signature <a
              href="/menu/entrees">Molcajete</a
            >, which brings grilled meats and vegetables together in a sizzling volcanic stone mortar.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="made-fresh-daily" class="v3-section v3-paper v3-scalloped" aria-labelledby="made-fresh-title">
      <div class="v3-scallop v3-scallop-red" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="v3-wrap v3-menu-split">
        <HomePhoto image={images.madeFreshDaily} class="v3-menu-split-photo" sizes="(min-width: 768px) 46vw, 100vw" />
        <div class="v3-menu-copy flex flex-col items-start gap-4">
          <h2 id="made-fresh-title" class="v3-display">Made Fresh Daily</h2>
          <p>Fresh preparation is part of our routine at El Ranchero.</p>
          <p>
            Each morning, our kitchen teams grill meats over an open-fire grill and prepare fresh vegetables and herbs.
            Our salsas are made in-house, ready to accompany the dishes served throughout the day.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you place an order, we assemble your food using ingredients prepared earlier that day. This allows us
            to serve tacos, burritos and other menu favorites efficiently while keeping daily preparation at the center
            of how we cook.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="local-partners" class="v3-section v3-menu-breakfast v3-center" aria-labelledby="local-partners-title">
      <ArtFlourish class="v3-art v3-art-flourish" aria-hidden="true" />
      <div class="v3-wrap">
        <div class="v3-ihead">
          <h2 id="local-partners-title" class="v3-display">Local Partners</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="v3-menu-copy flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-4">
          <p>Our daily preparation starts with ingredients supplied through local food distributors.</p>
          <p>
            We receive meats through a local distributor and work with a Hawaiʻi produce supplier for vegetables and
            other produce. From there, our kitchen teams prepare the ingredients used in our menu each day.
          </p>
          <p>
            These supplier relationships support our approach to serving freshly prepared food at both El Ranchero
            locations.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="the-murals" class="v3-section v3-paper v3-scalloped" aria-labelledby="murals-title">
      <div class="v3-scallop" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <ArtCactus class="v3-art v3-art-cactus" aria-hidden="true" />
      <div class="v3-wrap v3-menu-split v3-split-reverse">
        <HomePhoto image={images.murals} class="v3-menu-split-photo" sizes="(min-width: 768px) 46vw, 100vw" />
        <div class="v3-menu-copy flex flex-col items-start gap-4">
          <h2 id="murals-title" class="v3-display">The Murals</h2>
          <p>The chalk-art murals at El Ranchero are a visual connection between our two restaurants.</p>
          <p>
            Our Wahiawa location has a rustic, neighborhood taqueria atmosphere, while Kapolei offers a sit-down dining
            experience with table service and outdoor seating. Each restaurant has its own character, but the murals
            bring a recognizable part of El Ranchero into both spaces.
          </p>
          <p>
            They’re part of the setting guests experience when they visit us for a meal or spend an evening at the
            restaurant.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="community" class="v3-section" aria-labelledby="community-title">
      <div class="v3-wrap v3-menu-split v3-split-match">
        <HomePhoto image={images.givingBack} class="v3-menu-split-photo" sizes="(min-width: 768px) 46vw, 100vw" />
        <div class="v3-menu-copy flex flex-col items-start gap-4">
          <h2 id="community-title" class="v3-display">A Gathering Place for the Community</h2>
          <p>
            Our connection to Oʻahu goes beyond the food we serve. El Ranchero is also a gathering place for the
            island’s Latino community, with music and events that welcome everyone.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our regular programming includes karaoke, Latin Night and live concerts featuring Mexican bands. These
            gatherings bring people together around music and shared cultural experiences.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can explore our <a class="v3-link" href="/events">weekly events and upcoming performances</a> to see what’s
            happening at El Ranchero.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 flex flex-col items-start gap-3 sm:flex-row">
            <PosterButton text="Explore Our Menu" href="/menu" tone="gold" />
            <PosterButton text="Find a Location" href="/locations" tone="outline" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
